atlas provider
# External low-level capability organs (the external-repo rule): each is composed
# as a Bonfyre Provider via its LOWEST sensible boundary -- never ported in, never
# rewritten. They publish the facts (gates) that a physical asset's DERIVED
# capability depends on; a gate retracting (-1) withdraws the capability through
# the same DBSP circuit that maintains ReachableCapacity. maturity architectural:
# the repos are external and real, the Bonfyre boundary+wiring is the contract here.

architecture opencat-provider
  canonical_name OpenCatProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Device IO
  layer provider
  semantic_question By what serial/ESP32/ROS boundary does a quadruped produce physical state and accept commands?
  purpose External capability organ (Petoi OpenCat, ESP32 branch): gait coordination, servo control, IMU/sensor, telemetry, fleet examples. Composed as a Provider of device IO and telemetry; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  publishes DeviceTelemetry
  publishes ServoHealth
  forbidden_inference a device is connected -> its components are healthy (telemetry proves health, not reachability)
  interacts transport-phenotype
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is serial/ESP32/ROS device IO; the external firmware is real, the Bonfyre Provider binding is architectural

architecture kratos-provider
  canonical_name KratosProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Physics Simulation
  layer provider
  semantic_question What does a high-fidelity multiphysics run predict for this configuration and load?
  purpose External capability organ (KratosMultiphysics, C++ structural/fluid/FSI/DEM, OpenMP/MPI, CoSimIO). Composed as a physics-simulation Provider that emits a Simulation Receipt gating physical capability; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  consumes DesignCandidate
  publishes StructuralEnvelopeProof
  publishes ComponentFatigue
  forbidden_inference a simulation ran -> the physical asset is safe (a run predicts; a Receipt with its assumptions is the evidence)
  forbidden_inference model inference -> evidence
  interacts proof-frontier
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is C++/Python/MPI/CoSimIO; the framework is real, the Bonfyre Provider binding is architectural

architecture openmdao-provider
  canonical_name OpenMDAOProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Design Optimization
  layer provider
  semantic_question What design coordinates optimize a coupled multidisciplinary objective under constraints?
  purpose External capability organ (OpenMDAO, gradient-based coupled optimization over hundreds/thousands of design variables). Composed as a design-space Provider producing candidate coordinates; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  publishes DesignCandidate
  forbidden_inference a Pareto-optimal candidate -> a manufacturable or authorized one (feasibility/authority still gate)
  interacts kratos-provider
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is a native Python computational provider; the library is real, the Bonfyre binding is architectural

architecture carla-provider
  canonical_name CARLAProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Vehicle Simulation
  layer provider
  semantic_question Under what sensors, weather and autonomy mode is a route/vehicle configuration feasible?
  purpose External capability organ (CARLA autonomous-driving simulation, configurable sensors/weather, scenario+ROS hooks). Composed as a counterfactual Provider gating fleet dispatch; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  publishes RouteFeasibility
  forbidden_inference a simulated success -> a real delivery (a counterfactual run informs dispatch; the Receipt is reality)
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is the CARLA simulation API / ROS bridge; the simulator is real, the Bonfyre binding is architectural

architecture apparatus-provider
  canonical_name ApparatusProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Cyber Range
  layer provider
  semantic_question What cyber/network/chaos disturbance is being injected, and what fails under it?
  purpose External capability organ (Apparatus: attack/defense scenarios, honeypots, moving-target defense, chaos, protocols, PCAP/HAR replay, metrics/streams). Composed as a disturbance Provider emitting fault Occurrences; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  publishes NetworkFault
  publishes ChaosEvent
  forbidden_inference an injected fault survived -> the system is robust (one scenario is not the space)
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is HTTP/gRPC/SSE/WebSocket/CLI/metrics/PCAP; the range is real, the Bonfyre binding is architectural

architecture pace-provider
  canonical_name PACEProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Policy Doctrine
  layer provider
  semantic_question Given this event, what tiered rule of engagement, authority and escalation applies?
  purpose External capability organ (PACE doctrine: tiered ROE, cyber-physical mission dependencies, escalation-aware response). Composed as a Policy/Authority Provider making doctrine executable WITHOUT unrestricted autonomy; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  publishes ResponsePolicy
  consumes Authority
  forbidden_inference a doctrinal response is derived -> it is authorized to execute (the human gate and Authority still bind; reachability stops at the human line)
  interacts authority-graph
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is Policy/Authority/simulation rules (doctrine, not runtime code); making it executable is architectural

architecture mes-provider
  canonical_name MESProvider
  family provider
  domain Provider / Serialized Traceability
  layer provider
  semantic_question What is this serialized component's design, material batch, operations, inspection and disposition?
  purpose External capability organ (aerospace MES: serialized parts, assembly compatibility, FIFO allocation, roles, traceability, inventory). Composed as a digital-thread Provider of part provenance; never ported.
  maturity architectural
  publishes PartProvenance
  publishes MaterialBatch
  forbidden_inference a part is in inventory -> it is qualified for this assembly (compatibility + inspection still gate)
  interacts provider-graph
  source_lineage external low-level capability organ (external-repo rule)
  known_gap boundary is a domain fixture / REST / schema comparison; the MES is real, the Bonfyre binding is architectural

architecture physical-asset
  canonical_name PhysicalAssetGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Physical Asset
  layer provider
  semantic_question What can this physical asset actually do right now, derived from component health, proof, model and calibration?
  purpose A physical asset (robot, vehicle, cell) is a Bonfyre Resource whose capabilities are DERIVED, never statically declared: a capability is a conjunction of component-health / proof / model / calibration gates, maintained by the same DBSP circuit as ReachableCapacity. External Providers (OpenCat device IO, Kratos physics, CARLA, ...) supply the gates. A single telemetry -1 withdraws the capability incrementally, which is what stops WorkGraph assigning it and opens the maintenance cascade.
  maturity measured
  owns DerivedCapability
  derived DerivedCapability
  consumes DeviceTelemetry
  consumes ServoHealth
  consumes StructuralEnvelopeProof
  consumes ComponentFatigue
  consumes PartProvenance
  consumes MaterialBatch
  consumes RouteFeasibility
  consumes NetworkFault
  consumes ChaosEvent
  consumes ResponsePolicy
  publishes DerivedCapability
  internal_calculus multi-gate conjunction maintained in DBSP (capability reachable while all gates hold)
  invariant capability is derived from live gates, never statically declared
  invariant a component telemetry -1 withdraws the derived capability incrementally, with no rebuild
  forbidden_inference a device is connected -> the asset is capable (health/proof are derived, not assumed)
  forbidden_inference a capability advertised once -> still valid (it is maintained, and retracts on any gate -1)
  interacts opencat-provider
  interacts kratos-provider
  interacts feldera
  interacts work-graph
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/physical_asset.py
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_physical_asset.py
  source_lineage external-repo composition -- physical asset as derived-capability Resource
  known_gap proven for a robot climb capability through the live reachable_capacity DBSP circuit (telemetry -1 -> capability withdrawn); binding real OpenCat telemetry + Kratos proofs at the device boundary is the external-provider wiring
